      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Meckel's diverticulum (MD) is the most frequent congenital abnormality of the small bowel and it is often difficult to diagnose. The authors report a case of a patient with long-term symptoms erroneously not related with MD disease and developing a diverticulum perforation."},
